                    "properties": {
                        "metisFindingId": "c1bbe3103a0d4c17906ca8f876cd1ef3",
                        "cwe": "CWE-362",
                        "severity": "Medium",
                        "reasoning": "The file keeps per-component FMP header and received-image counters in global state. This state is initialized only by fmp_header_image_info_init() during fwu_bootloader_init(), but failed, rejected, aborted, or completed update flows shown in this file do not reset fmp_hdr_size_recvd or image_size_recvd for the component. Subsequent firmware update attempts in the same boot can therefore reuse stale fw_version/header data or stale image_size_recvd offsets. For example, fwu_bootloader_load_image skips header parsing once fmp_hdr_size_recvd equals the header size and writes at image_offset + image_size_recvd. This can cause later uploads to be written at the wrong offset or evaluated against an old version, potentially corrupting staged images or bypassing intended update sequencing. Reachability depends on higher-level FWU session management, but the state lifetime issue is visible in this file.",
                        "mitigation": "Reset fmp_header_image_info for a component at the start of a new staging operation, after install/reject/abort, and on any load error. Track explicit transaction/session state so stale per-component counters cannot affect subsequent updates.",
                        "confidence": 0.72,
                        "anchor": {
                            "file_path": "platform/ext/target/arm/corstone1000/bootloader/mcuboot/tfm_mcuboot_fwu.c",
                            "start_line": 329,
                            "end_line": 330,
